# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# RAMCES — .gitignore
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Every line of this file used to be commented out, which means NOTHING was
# ignored — including `.env`, which holds the real SECRET_KEY, the database
# password and the bootstrap admin password. A single `git add -A` would have
# committed all three. (Checked: `.env` never entered history, so this is a near
# miss and not a cleanup.)
#
# Two things a .gitignore cannot do, so they are done by hand:
#   * it does NOT untrack a file that is already tracked — use
#     `git rm --cached <path>` for that;
#   * it does NOT scrub history — if a secret is ever committed, rotate it.


# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.env` is required to boot: DATABASE_URL and SECRET_KEY have no fallbacks and
# the app refuses to start without them. `.env.example` documents every key
# with no values and IS tracked, so the negation below must stay after the glob.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/


# ── Runtime data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Calibration certificates, Model/Type photos and reference documents uploaded
# through the app, plus the copies the `dokumen` seed step writes. ~64 MB today
# and it only grows. Regenerate with `py -3.10 seed.py --only dokumen`.
uploads/


# ── The client's source drop ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `modules/` is ~41 MB: the katalog spreadsheets, the asset import workbook and
# roughly 40 MB of manual/spektek PDFs.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS A HARD DEPENDENCY, NOT AN OPTIONAL EXTRA. Since rev0.5.2,
# `seed_katalog_sfm.py` reads `KATALOG SFM.xlsx` directly and `seed_katalog.py`
# RAISES on import without it — deliberately, because the previous behaviour
# was to import cleanly and silently produce an empty catalogue, which made the
# asset import skip all 1,121 rows while reporting success.
#
# A fresh checkout can serve the app (the API and SPA do not import these
# modules) but cannot seed or reset until `modules/` is copied in.
modules/


# ── Database dumps and scratch ────────────────────────────────────────
sql_backup/
temp/
*.sql
*.dump
*.bak

# Route/OpenAPI snapshots written by tools/verify/snap.py. The harness itself is
# tracked (see tools/verify/README.md); its output is not — a snapshot is a
# before/after comparison artefact, meaningful only within one run.
tools/verify/_snapshots/
*.snapshot.json

# Belt and braces: a headless-Chrome profile is ~300 files of caches, cookies and
# shader blobs. cdp.py now writes them to the system temp dir, but one earlier
# run put a full profile inside tools/verify/ and it very nearly got committed.
chrome-profile-*/


# ── Editors, tooling, OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# The seeding pipeline — `seed.py`, `reset.py`, `seeds/`, `seed_katalog.py`,
# `seed_katalog_sfm.py`, `seed_aset_real.py` — is TRACKED.
#
# It used to be ignored. That was a mistake and it cost real review coverage:
# `seed_katalog.py` is tracked while `seeds/katalog.py` was not, so gutting the
# first and rewiring the second showed up in git as exactly half a change. It is
# ~2,300 lines of ordinary source with no secrets in it (the only `secrets`
# import is the stdlib module used to generate the bootstrap password), it
# decides whether 1,121 real assets import correctly, and `reset.py` is the most
# destructive command in the project. All three are reasons to review it, not
# reasons to hide it.
#
# `api/`, `tools/`, `CLAUDE.md` and `.env.example` are also tracked and were
# simply never `git add`ed — see the notes for the next session.
